{# ONE CHIP OF THE HOUSE FILTER BAR (`.lfilt`).

   A CLOSED CHIP THAT OPENS A PANEL OF OPTIONS WITH LIVE COUNTS — the
   incidents pattern, which is the standing rule for every filter bar in the
   product.

   IT IS A `<details>`, AND EVERY OPTION IS A LINK. The address is the state,
   so a filtered list is a link somebody can send and a page a browser can go
   back to; and the whole control opens, chooses and clears with no script of
   ours, which is what keeps a filter bar working on a page that has none.

   AN OPTION IS A VALUE, A LABEL, A COUNT AND SOMETIMES A COLOUR. A role
   filters by the word it is spelt with; a zone filters by an identifier and
   reads as a name with its own hue. One control serves both because the
   caller hands it {@see Uhifadhi\Bundle\AreaBundle\Model\FilterOption}s
   rather than a map it would have to guess the shape of. An option whose
   count is null (an order) draws none.

   THE CLOSED CHIP NAMES THE CHOSEN OPTION AND ITS COUNT ("western sector ·
   4"), or the "all" option and its count while nothing is chosen.

   THE COUNTS ARE OF THE WHOLE SET, not of what is already filtered: a count
   that moved as you filtered could not tell you what picking an option would
   do, which is the one thing it is for.

   THE LINKS. A page whose question is a query model hands it over as
   `query` (`query.with(key, value)`); a page whose question is the address
   itself leaves `query` out, and the link is the request's own query with
   this key changed and `pageKey` (`page` when absent) dropped, so a second
   table on the page keeps its own place. The page size is kept either way.

   An axis with no "all" (a month) passes `all: null`.

   Takes: key, all, allCount?, label? (the menu's head), chosen, chosenLabel?,
   options, query? | pageKey?. #}
{% set _route = app.request.attributes.get('_route') %}
{% set _params = app.request.attributes.get('_route_params') %}
{% set _pageKey = pageKey ?? 'page' %}
{% set _query = query ?? null %}
{% set _here = app.request.query.all|filter((v, k) => k != key and k != _pageKey) %}
{% set _per = _query is not null and app.request.query.has('per') ? {per: app.request.query.get('per')} : {} %}
{% set _chosenOption = chosen is null ? null : options|filter(o => o.value == chosen)|first %}
{% set _picked = chosenLabel ?? (_chosenOption ? _chosenOption.label : chosen) %}
{% set _count = chosen is null ? (allCount ?? null) : (_chosenOption ? _chosenOption.count : null) %}
<details class="i-dd">
    <summary class="mchip i-ddt{{ chosen is not null ? ' on' : '' }}">
        <span class="i-ddval">{{ (_picked is not null ? _picked : all|raw)|lower }}{% if _count is not null %} &middot; {{ _count }}{% endif %}</span>
        <span class="i-ddcaret">&#9662;</span>
    </summary>
    <div class="i-ddmenu" aria-label="{{ label ?? key }}">
        {% if label is defined and label is not null %}<span class="i-ddhead">{{ label|raw }}</span>{% endif %}
        {% if all is not null %}
        <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosen is null ? ' on' : '' }}"
           href="{{ path(_route, _params|merge(_query is not null ? _query.with(key, null)|merge(_per) : _here)) }}">
            <span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ all|raw }}</span>
            {% if allCount is defined and allCount is not null %}<span class="i-ddopt-n">{{ allCount }}</span>{% endif %}
        </a>
        <span class="i-ddsep"></span>
        {% endif %}
        {% for option in options %}
            <a class="i-ddopt{{ chosen is not null and chosen == option.value ? ' on' : '' }}"
               href="{{ path(_route, _params|merge(_query is not null ? _query.with(key, option.value)|merge(_per) : _here|merge({(key): option.value}))) }}">
                {% if option.cat ?? null %}<span class="i-dot" data-cat="{{ option.cat }}"></span>{% endif %}
                <span class="i-ddopt-l">{{ option.label }}</span>
                {% if option.count is not null %}<span class="i-ddopt-n">{{ option.count }}</span>{% endif %}
            </a>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
</details>
